                <pb facs="0855" n="743" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg743"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Consul Moffat</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-03-08"><hi rendition="#italic">March 8,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Knox acknowledges Mr. Moffat’s telegram of March 3 and directs him to say to
                    Gen. Estrada and the leaders of the revolution that the Government of the United
                    States is not disposed at this time to make any suggestion in response to a
                    unilateral representation.</p>
            </div>
